<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balšić noble family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Balšići, House of Balšić</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balšić were a noble family that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a>, roughly present-day Montenegro and northern Albania, from about 1360 to 1421 after the break-up of the Serbian Empire. From their seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a> they fought Ragusa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and Albanian lords. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii">Balša II</a> was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at Savra in 1385, and when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-iii">Balša III</a> died in 1421 the line ended and Zeta passed to the Serbian Despotate.</p></div>
